# Documentation Governance

Documentation supports traceability — it is **not** a substitute for implementation.

## When Documentation Updates Are Required

Update authoritative docs when changes affect:

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Architecture / layer boundaries | `ARCHITECTURE-STACK.md`, ADR in `.cursor/architecture/adr/`, `GOVERNANCE-MAP.md` if mapping shifts |
| New architectural decision | ADR (mandatory) |
| API contract | `api-conventions.md`, module docs, OpenAPI if present |
| Database schema semantics | `database-blueprint.md`, `database-dictionary.md`, migration notes per `database-change` skill |
| Module boundaries | `MODULE-CONTRACT.md`, `docs/sis/{module}/` |
| Runtime / platform / UI contracts | `RUNTIME-CONTRACT.md`, `PLATFORM-CONTRACT.md`, `UI-CONTRACT.md`, `WINDOW-CONTRACT.md` |
| Security baseline | `.cursor/security/SECURITY-BASELINE.json`, security phase docs |
| Major UI behavior | UI contract + module gate report if phased |

## Also Required When Applicable

- Schema change impact (`schema-change-impact.md`) for DB changes
- Completion / gate report (`docs/sis/` or phase folder) for gated work
- **SIS CHANGE REPORT** per Constitution §81 for significant tasks

## Not Required For

- Typo fixes with no contract impact
- Pure refactors with identical external behavior (unless architecture graph changes)
- Governance-only typo fixes with no precedence/mapping change

## Rule

If you change what another developer or agent must know to use the system safely, update the doc **in the same change** — do not defer documentation to avoid finishing implementation.
